    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0259",
      "sequence": 271,
      "meaning": "The bee of speech is trapped in her lotus mouth, unable to emerge on seeing the night of modesty. Tears remain in the corners of her eyes like a supreme miser’s gold. Deeply aware of her anxious reserve, Sītā gathers courage and brings faith into her heart: if my vow in body, mind and speech is true and my heart is absorbed in Raghupati’s lotus feet, then the Lord who dwells in every heart will make me Raghubīra’s servant. Whoever bears true love for another surely meets the beloved; there is no doubt. She fixes love in her body while gazing upon the Lord, and Rāma, treasury of compassion, knows everything. Looking at Sītā, he regards the bow as Garuḍa regards a little serpent. Lakṣmaṇa recognizes the jewel of Raghu’s line looking toward Hara’s bow; thrilled throughout his body, he presses down the universe with his feet and speaks.",
